s-0292-6bab6a7ad6da:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"Larry Gilbert\", \"scope\": \"Sport association\", \"claim\": \"Larry Gilbert is associated with golf, as evidenced by his wins in the PGA Club Professional Championship, Kentucky PGA Championships, Kentucky Opens, Tennessee Open, and Tennessee PGA Championship, and his induction into the Kentucky Golf Hall of Fame.\", \"answer\": \"Golf\", \"quote\": \"He won the PGA Club Professional Championship in 1981, 1982 and 1991. He also won ten Kentucky PGA Championships, three Kentucky Opens, one Tennessee Open and one Tennessee PGA Championship. Gilbert was inducted into the Kentucky Golf Hall of Fame in 1992; he is also a member of the Middle Tennessee State University Athletics Hall of Fame. He joined the Senior PGA Tour (later known as the Champions Tour) upon turning 50 in 1992.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0292-6bab6a7ad6da:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0292-6bab6a7ad6da:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"Larry Gilbert\", \"scope\": \"sport association\", \"claim\": \"Larry Gilbert was an American right fielder in Major League Baseball.\", \"answer\": \"baseball\", \"quote\": \"Larry Gilbert (baseball) Lawrence William Gilbert (December 3, 1891 – February 17, 1965) was an American right fielder in Major League Baseball and a longtime manager in minor league baseball.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0292-6bab6a7ad6da:d02\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0292-6bab6a7ad6da:d02:c0\", \"entity\": \"Larry Gilbert\", \"scope\": \"sport association\", \"claim\": \"Larry Gilbert is associated with baseball, as indicated by the text mentioning 'Boston Braves Larry Gilbert Minor Leagues' and the author identifying as a 'baseball historian'.\", \"answer\": \"baseball\", \"quote\": \"Posted in Grave Story Boston Braves Larry Gilbert Minor Leagues Nashville Volunteers New Orleans New Orleans Pelicans Published by Sam Gazdziak I am a professional journalist , baseball historian and cemetery search